  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1245 PM CDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nConvective evolution Friday through Saturday is uncertain as the\nregion transitions from the post frontal regime to the prevailing\nwarm sector by Sunday. Various guidance members suggest storm\ncoverage expands Thursday night into Friday morning north of the\nboundary before spreading east of the region by Friday evening. A\nlull in storm potential is likely Friday night into early Saturday\nbefore a potential storm complex develops and propagates on the\nperiphery of the persistent upper ridge and potentially spread\ninto NE OK or NW AR Saturday. Timing and details of storm\npotential Friday through Saturday will continue to be refined.\n\nThe predominant pattern through next week will be the persistent\nupper ridge centered in or near the local region. A potential cold\nfront early next week may offer another chance of showers and\nstorms, but no obvious airmass change is currently see and\nexpectations remain for temperatures well above seasonal normals \nto persist.",
